  "mode": "dist",
  "supersedes": null,
  "requires": {
    "sm": 90,
    "gpus": 2,
    "env": "triton-dist"
  },
  "timeout_s": 900,
  "notes": [
    "Tutorial 06 of Triton-distributed 7908e4ea (inter-node reduce-scatter): reduce_scatter_2d_op, unchanged, on a 512 x 128 bfloat16 matrix per rank, 2 ranks. one_node/* is the control under triton-dist; logical_nodes/* runs 2 logical nodes of 1 rank.",
    "Expected, judged on the development side only (experiments/interp_gpu/internode_logical/judge.py): the first three tests ok, every rank returning its 256 rows of the sum of both inputs.",
    "PREDICTED FAILURE, wanted as a result: logical_nodes/tutorial_context builds the context with the tutorial's own create_reduce_scater_2d_ctx, which indexes the tensors of the rank's node with the global rank (line 202 of the tutorial). Rank 1 is expected to end with \"IndexError: list index out of range\" before any kernel runs; rank 0 is then expected to wait for it until the 240 s timeout of that test. Status runtime_error or timeout is the expected outcome of that test, not a fault of the GPU side; a retry would end the same way.",
    "*/harness_context builds the same context in the harness with that one index taken within the node.",
    "Meant for an NVLink pair, as internode-logical-env-002 ran on: under logical nodes the tutorial's barrier uses atomic operations on the peer's memory without asking the driver whether the pair supports them."
  ],
